  "description": "The HIGH-VALUES anchor, preserved exactly as it behaves (practice B5). CDEMO-CU00-USRID-LAST arrives blank while NEXT-PAGE-YES arrives 'Y', so :263 anchors the browse on HIGH-VALUES. GTEQ is commented out at :592, which selects the default STARTBR positioning it would have asked for, and no key can be at or after high values - so a request to page FORWARD reports NOTFND and paints 'You are at the top of the page...'. That arm raises no error flag, so :286 lets PROCESS-PAGE-FORWARD continue: :288 holds for PF8, a READNEXT is issued against a browse that was never established, and because its outcome is neither NORMAL nor ENDFILE the WHEN OTHER arm at :641-647 raises the error flag and overwrites the message with 'Unable to lookup User...'. :327-:329 still run, because they sit inside the IF that opened at :286 and closes at :331, so the page number is written and the map sent a third time. Two messages, in that order, and the final image carries the second: this is the case that proves the guard at :288 tests the error flag alone and nothing about end of file.",
